# Data — never committed. See ADR-0007.
# Inputs (mirrored copies of other systems' files) and producer observations
# are data. The distilled registries (principles/, habits/) are SYSTEM and
# tracked in git per ADR-0018 — adopted canon is part of the system, not data.

# NO trailing slash on these five. A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, and in a
# poga lane these paths are SYMLINKS to the main checkout's copies (session 90) — which
# git sees as symlinks, not directories, so `users/` let `users` through as untracked and
# the machine-specific link would have been committed. Without the slash the pattern
# matches the directory and the symlink alike.
inputs
users
architect-learnings.md
retrofit-reports
proposed-edits

# Python bytecode — build artifacts from running the harness/tests, never committed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local-only working files
*.local.md
scratch/
snapshots/

# Machine-local reconcile search roots (P3 — machine-specific paths stay out of
# git). reconcile-roots.example is tracked as the template; the .local copy is not.
# See curate/reconcile.py --status.
reconcile-roots.local

# Machine-local system-id -> repo-path locator map (P3). repo-paths.example is
# tracked as the template; the .local copy is not. See curate/reconcile.py.
repo-paths.local

# Machine-local poga wrapper hooks (WI-0028 — the board ensure
# command carries a machine-specific path and port, P3). poga.local.example is
# tracked as the template; the .local copy is not. Sourced by poga_board_ensure.
poga.local

# Curate-pass generated review files — ephemeral staging output. The gather
# script (curate/gather.py) and its cursor (curate/seen.json) are system and
# tracked; the REVIEW-*.md files it generates are throwaway. See ADR-0019.
curate-runs/

# Metrics evidence appendix (ADR-0048) — a reproducible, on-demand mined snapshot
# (curate/metrics.py --evidence). Regenerated for the case study when needed; not a
# source of truth, so it is not tracked (avoids churn on every regen). The generator
# and fleet-cadence.json ARE system and tracked; this rendered output is a build
# artifact. The guard-firing log it reads lives under .session-state/ (below).
EVIDENCE.md

# Claude Code: machine-local settings overrides + transient agent worktrees.
# Project settings (.claude/settings.json) are system and committed; the
# files below are user-machine-specific or transient and must not be.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Session liveness sidecar (ADR-0036) — ephemeral, machine-local, all-derivable
# heartbeat/ended markers keyed by session_id. Evidence for orphan triage only;
# never authoritative (the tracked start stamp is). Must not be committed.
.session-state/

# Concrete rendered adoption-runner LaunchAgent (ADR-0050): the installer fills the
# tracked deploy/*.template with this machine's absolute paths (P3) and installs to
# ~/Library/LaunchAgents. A stray filled plist under deploy/ must never be committed.
deploy/*.plist

# Machine-local deploy seed sources (P3 / ADR-0103 — where a first deploy copies a
# system's gitignored state from on THIS machine). seed-paths.local.example.json is
# tracked as the template; the .local copy is not. Read by deploy/runner.py.
deploy/seed-paths.local.json

# Machine-local deploy ledger lives OUTSIDE the repo entirely
# (~/.local/state/poga/deploy) — nothing to ignore here, noted so the next reader
# does not go looking for it in-tree.

# PUBLIC CUT: these hold what the cut publishes (the sample, the blank
# profile), so the internal data rules above are lifted for them.
!users
